WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.797 --> 00:00:03.380
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:10.980
- Yale Class of 2021, congratulations.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:12.220
Samantha Power here.

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:14.840
I've been asked to keep
it short and keep it fun.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.390
If anyone knows how to
keep it short and fun,

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:22.299
it's me, the author of a
700 page book on genocide.

00:00:22.299 --> 00:00:25.420
But in all seriousness,
I hope you graduate today

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:28.870
with a heart full of pride,
a head full of smarts,

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:32.140
and a commitment to defend
dignity wherever you go.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:33.790
Yours, and that of the people

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:36.300
in the world less fortunate than you.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.920
COVID-19 has taken so much from us,

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.830
but it's also given us something:

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:43.220
a broadened sense of empathy.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:47.150
This is a rare moment in time,
when everyone on planet earth

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:50.554
has had their lives changed together.

00:00:50.554 --> 00:00:55.290
We all got a lesson in what
essential really means.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:58.480
As you leave Yale today,
and this pandemic breaks,

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:01.720
I urge you not to lose that empathy.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:05.400
Your concern for a world
outside of your own is the key

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.880
to living that big,
fulfilling life that you seek.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.840
Congratulations, Yale Class of 2021.

